"│     ▼ [a] What happens to a borrow when the owner  ││ ── reasoning ──                                                │"
"│         answer                                     ││ Let me think about what a move does to a borrow.               │"
"│     ▶ [x] Why can't a &mut and a & borrow coexist? ││ The borrow checker tracks every live reference to the owner.   │"
"│       [ ] When does NLL end a borrow?              ││ A move invalidates the owner's place, so no borrow may outlive │"
"│   ▶ Lifetimes  1 q, 1 a                            ││ it.                                                            │"
"│   ▶ (missing subtopic)  1 q, 1 a                   ││ ── answer ──                                                   │"
"│   traits  0 sub, 0 q, 0 a                          ││ The borrow must end before the move.                           │"
"│ ▶ (not configured) old_topic  1 sub, 1 q, 1 a      ││ If a reference is still used after the move, the compiler      │"
"│                                                    ││ reports E0505: cannot move out of the value because it is      │"
"│                                                    ││ borrowed.                                                      │"
"│                                                    ││ Non-lexical lifetimes end a borrow at its last use, not at the │"
"│                                                    ││ end of its scope, so many such programs compile.               │"
